      },
      "rev_n_1_321885_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_321885_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_321885",
        "thought_text": "Identify the current GCD of all numbers and consider replacing each number with a multiple of the largest prime factor of any number in the set to maximize the new GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_321885_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_d79170d296",
        "created_at": 1794500254.0564942
      },
      "rev_n_2_863c5e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_863c5e_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_863c5e",
        "thought_text": "Focus on the smallest number and try to make it a multiple of the product of the prime factors of the other numbers to increase the overall GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_863c5e_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e5aa14723a",
        "created_at": 1794500272.0512402
      },
      "rev_n_3_e5abf8_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_e5abf8_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_e5abf8",
        "thought_text": "Thought-1 (revised): Instead of replacing the smallest number with the highest power of 2, consider replacing each number with the highest power of 2 that divides it. This approach ensures that the GCD can potentially increase significantly if multiple numbers share common factors.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_e5abf8_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_34777b0325",
        "created_at": 1794500279.0099332
      },
      "rev_n_4_edd80e_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_edd80e_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_edd80e",
        "thought_text": "The current approach focuses on checking multiples of primes up to 10, which may not always yield the optimal result. We need to explore a more comprehensive method to find the maximum possible GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-306766479340521810",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500301.1059322
      },
      "rev_n_5_36f9bb_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_36f9bb_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_36f9bb",
        "thought_text": "Instead of modifying each number individually, we can consider the properties of the GCD itself. Specifically, we can look at the highest power of each prime that divides any of the numbers in the array, as this could lead to a higher overall GCD when modified.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-306766479340521810",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500301.105948
      },
      "rev_n_6_79dac4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_79dac4_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_79dac4",
        "thought_text": "We should also consider the possibility of setting all numbers to the same value, as this might simplify the problem and allow us to easily calculate the maximum possible GCD.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-306766479340521810",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500301.1059566
      },
      "rev_n_5_36f9bb_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_36f9bb_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_36f9bb",
        "thought_text": "Consider the highest power of each prime that divides any of the numbers in the array. When you replace a number with a multiple of this highest power, the resulting GCD will be maximized. However, ensure that the replacement does not exceed \\(10^9\\).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-306766479340521810",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_36f9bb_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_2ad8316c6f",
        "created_at": 1794500319.2388287
      },
      "rev_n_7_8d929f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_8d929f_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_8d929f",
        "thought_text": "Replace the smallest number with its double.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-6323394256425791867",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794500336.5998178
      },
      "rev_n_8_08e7b5_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_08e7b5_0",
